Z||000002||Greg Piet||04-09-2001||01:39 PM||||Reminds me of the following(which is not entirely verbatim to the way I heard it)...<P>There are no physicists in the hottest parts of hell.  The reason being is that a hottest part implies a temperature differential, and any marginally competant physicist would build a heat engine to make some part of hell comfortably cool.<BR>  <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72 Race Director<BR>#47 CSP<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.physics.unlv.edu/~gregpiet/Jan1617s.jpg">   <BR>Our lady of blessed acceleration dont fail me now!||||reg||1
